.TH CCENV 1 "2026-05-01" "ccenv 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ccenv \- profile manager and usage analytics for Claude Code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ccenv
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ccenv
manages multiple Claude Code provider profiles and tracks token usage across sessions.
.PP
Each profile is a TOML file under
.I ~/.config/ccenv/profiles/
containing the environment variables needed to point Claude Code at an Anthropic-compatible API.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ccenv
Launch claude with an interactive profile picker.
.TP
.BI "ccenv [" name ]
Switch to
.I name
and launch claude.
.TP
.BI "ccenv add [" name ]
Create a new profile interactively. Prompts for name, provider, model, auth token, and description.
.TP
.BI "ccenv use [" name ]
Switch the current profile without launching claude. Opens a picker if no name is provided.
.TP
.B ccenv list
List all profiles. Current profile is marked with
.BR * .
.TP
.B ccenv current
Show the current profile name and effective environment variables.
.TP
.BI "ccenv remove [" name ]
Delete a profile. Opens a picker if no name is provided.
.TP
.BI "ccenv edit [" name ]
Open a profile file in
.BR $EDITOR .
Defaults to the current profile.
.TP
.B --reset
Regenerate the profile from its built-in template before opening the editor.
.TP
.B ccenv stats
Show token usage from Claude Code session logs. Defaults to model-based grouping.
.TP
.B ccenv man
Open this man page.
.SH STATS OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--since " window
Time window:
.BR 7d " (default), " 30d ", " 90d ", " 365d ", or " YYYY-MM-DD .
.TP
.B --project
Group by project instead of model.
.TP
.B --json
Machine-readable JSON output.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Profiles are stored in
.IR ~/.config/ccenv/profiles/ .
The current profile name is stored in
.IR ~/.config/ccenv/current .
.PP
Profile files use TOML format:
.PP
.RS
.nf
description = "My provider"

[env]
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL = "https://api.example.com"
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN = "${MY_API_KEY}"
ANTHROPIC_MODEL = "model-name"
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B ${ENV_VAR}
placeholders in
.B ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN
are resolved from the shell environment at launch time.
.SH BUILT-IN PROVIDERS
.TS
l l l.
Provider	Type	Base URL
_
